HB0115 Medical Ethics Defense Act.
Sponsored By: Representative(s) Ottman, Schmid, Singh and Styvar
and Senator(s) Hutchings, Ide, Pearson and Steinmetz
AN ACT relating to public health and safety; allowing health care providers,
health care institutions and health care payers the right to refuse to
participate in or pay for health care services as specified; authorizing
religious-based health care organizations to make decisions consistent with
religious beliefs; prohibiting discrimination for making health care decisions
based on conscience; prohibiting adverse licensing actions based on protected
expressive activity; specifying liability and damages for notice requirements;
providing immunity; providing definitions; specifying applicability; requiring
rulemaking; and providing for effective dates.
